  {
   "id": 68,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    0,
    820
   ],
   "size": [
    500,
    470
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 9,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "Read me - speed, settings, edit tips + low VRAM",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Speed (tested, RTX 4000 Ada 20 GB, int8 set)\n- **Use PyTorch for CUDA 13 (cu130).** On CUDA 12.8 it was about 3.5x slower.\n- 4 MP edit: ~35 s sampling. Prompt upsampler: ~10-15 s. 5 pictures in one edit: ~5.5 min.\n\n## Settings (official, already set)\n8 steps (Manual Sigmas), euler, no CFG (Basic Guider), sigma shift 1 / 1.\n\n## Edit tips\n- Picture 1 is the image to edit. Call the pictures `<Picture 1>`, `<Picture 2>` ... in your instruction.\n- **Edit size:** 4 MP default, 8 MP max (Pruna: edits work best at 4 or 8 MP). The edit keeps Picture 1's aspect ratio.\n- **References:** turn Pictures 2-5 on in the toggle panel. Up to 8 pictures in total: connect another Load Image to the next free input on p-h3-image Conditioning and Batch Images. Each picture adds time.\n- **Prompt upsampler on:** a short instruction is enough. **Off:** your instruction goes to the model as written, so describe the result in detail.\n- **Image Scale By** doubles the saved image (lanczos). Set it to 1 to save at the edit size.\n\n## Low VRAM (tested by capping the VRAM on a 20 GB card)\n- Load the w4a8 model and the w4a8 text encoder: full speed at an 8 GB and a 6 GB cap.\n- At the 6 GB cap a 4 MP edit took ~36 s and peaked at ~5.3 GB.\n- The prompt upsampler slows to ~30-50 s under a cap. ComfyUI used up to ~17.5 GB of system RAM."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## Speed (tested, RTX A4500 20 GB)\n- **Use the CUDA 13 build of PyTorch** (NVIDIA driver 580+). On CUDA 12.8 the int8 / w4a8 fast kernels stay off: a 4 MP image took 86 s instead of 20 s (measured on an RTX 4000 Ada).\n- No Comfy Kitchen attention node needed: these model files already use it.\n- **2-step LoRA group** (off by default): 16 MP sampling 19 s instead of 57 s, an edit 9 s instead of 27 s. At 100% it leaves a fine mesh, so use it for drafts and the full 6 steps for finals. Keep the LoRA at exactly 1.0.\n\n## Settings (tested)\n- **euler / simple / 6 steps / CFG 1** - the model is distilled to exactly this.\n- **Do NOT use karras, dpmpp_2m or res_multistep** - they break the image with no error.\n- euler_ancestral looks more natural on fur/skin but can **scramble small text** - keep euler for anything with words.\n- Low VRAM: load **minimax_h3_image_pruned_w4a8** in the model loader. With the VRAM capped at 8 GB and at 6 GB it kept full speed on an RTX A4500 (16 MP 58 s, edit 28 s, peak 5.9 GiB at the 6 GB cap). System RAM is the catch: my runs used 45-50 GB, so **32 GB may be tight** (it can run out of memory) but should still work. Turn the Prompt Expander off on low VRAM.\n\n## Edit tips (tested)\n- 4 MP default (~27 s sampling, ~43 s per edit on an RTX A4500), **8 MP max, never 16 MP** for edits.\n- **Half-done edit? Change the seed first.** Still stubborn (removals, whole-scene changes)? **Edit at 1 MP.**\n- References: Pictures 2-5 here; add more Load Image nodes for up to 16 (the expander only sees Pictures 1-4). **Crop busy photos** - Picture 1 is the image to edit.\n- 5 pictures: ~3 min sampling on an RTX A4500. Each extra picture costs time, not VRAM.\n- Expander ON = type a short instruction (~124 s per edit). OFF = write a detailed prompt yourself (~43 s)."
   },
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
